{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1749369,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"light-blue-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"Robo Race","festival_id":476371,"organization_id":406444,"web_url":"www.ioittenet.com\/","start_date":"2026-09-12T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-23T17:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/robo-race-tenet-aissms-institute-of-information-technology-pune-maharashtra-1749369","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Ready. Set. Race. <\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Put your robot to the ultimate test in <strong>Robo Race<\/strong>, a high-energy robotics competition designed to challenge <strong>speed, precision, maneuverability, stability, and real-world robot control<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>Navigate your robot through a challenging obstacle track featuring <strong>sharp turns, zig-zag sections, ramps, bridges, rough terrain, speed breakers, and other obstacles<\/strong>. Every second counts, but precision matters&mdash;penalties for missed checkpoints, resets, and going off-course will add to your final time.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Event Structure<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>09:00 AM:<\/strong> Reporting &amp; Registration<\/li>\n<li><strong>09:30 AM onwards:<\/strong> Competition Begins<\/li>\n<li><strong>Practice Attempt:<\/strong> One practice run for each team<\/li>\n<li><strong>Official Run:<\/strong> One timed attempt considered for scoring<\/li>\n<li><strong>Final Result:<\/strong> Based on the lowest adjusted completion time<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Participation Categories<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"355\"><strong data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"260\">Team &ndash; Organizer Bot:<\/strong> For teams of 1&ndash;4 members using an organizer-provided bot. <strong data-start=\"319\" data-end=\"355\">Registration Fee: \u20b9149 per team.<\/strong><\/li>\n<li data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"470\"><strong data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"376\">Team &ndash; Own Bot:<\/strong> For teams of 1&ndash;4 members using their own race-ready bot. <strong data-start=\"434\" data-end=\"470\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Registration Fee: \u20b9199 per team.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Participants bringing their own robot must ensure that it meets the specified technical and safety requirements. An organizer-provided robot option is also available for solo participants.<\/p>\n<p><strong>\ufe0f Key Specifications<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Maximum Robot Size:<\/strong> 30 &times; 30 &times; 30 cm<\/li>\n<li><strong>Maximum Weight:<\/strong> 5 kg<\/li>\n<li><strong>Maximum Voltage:<\/strong> 12V DC<\/li>\n<li><strong>Control:<\/strong> Wired or Wireless<\/li>\n<li><strong>Mobility:<\/strong> Wheel- or track-based<\/li>\n<li><strong>Power:<\/strong> On-board battery only<\/li>\n<li><strong>Robot:<\/strong> Student-built or student-integrated<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Participants can compete <strong>solo or in teams of 2&ndash;4<\/strong>&nbsp;and may bring their own eligible robot or opt for an organizer-provided robot where applicable.<\/p>\n<p><strong>What Awaits You?<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>\ufe0fRace through a challenging obstacle track<\/li>\n<li>Test your robot's speed and maneuverability<\/li>\n<li>\ufe0fApply practical robotics, electronics, and control skills<\/li>\n<li>Navigate checkpoints with precision<\/li>\n<li>Minimize penalties and beat the clock<\/li>\n<li>Compete against robotics enthusiasts from across colleges<\/li>\n<li>The winner will get a trophy, and certificates will be given to all the participants<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Trophy & \u20b910,000 Prize Pool for winners. Certificates will be awarded to all participating teams.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27539330,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:28:09+05:30","updated_at":"2026-09-30T14:39:28+05:30","communication_sent":6,"certificate_at":nul